# The build context is tarred and sent to the Docker daemon before anything
# else runs — without this file that tar ships the host's macOS/arm64
# node_modules (breaks native binaries like sharp inside a linux image),
# every dist/.next build output, and every .env secret. Mirrors .gitignore,
# but Docker doesn't read .gitignore on its own — this file is separate and
# required.
#
# Every pattern below has BOTH a bare form and a `**/` form — confirmed the
# hard way (M13 code review): unlike .gitignore, a bare pattern in
# .dockerignore only matches at the context ROOT, not at any depth. Without
# the `**/` form, apps/event-processor/.env (real RabbitMQ/DB config, not a
# placeholder) got copied into the image and silently overrode a container
# env var at runtime — an actual live bug, not a style nit. Never assume a
# bare pattern here is recursive.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
coverage
**/coverage
.git
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.omc
**/.omc

*.env
**/*.env
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
